<!--
  The four pages a stranger can read.

  The console, an invitation and a collection link are deliberately absent. They are
  behind a session or a single-use token, so a crawler could only be told they exist and
  never shown them — and this platform's promise is that a distribution link reaches one
  person rather than a search index. `/console` is the sharper case: without a session it
  renders the sign-in sheet, so listing it would advertise a page whose only content is
  "sign in".

  No `lastmod`, and no `changefreq` or `priority` either. `lastmod` is supposed to be the
  date the page's content changed, and a build timestamp is not that: a sitemap that says
  "changed today" on every deploy is a sitemap a crawler learns to ignore. The other two
  are documented as ignored by Google, so writing them would be writing decoration.
-->
